From ba4a56fab6a2426ec3cacaed4889830eae56135f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrosha <114847463+JRoshangah@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:51:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Add board-first match layout with Navy Gold styling

- Separate layout file (match_arena.xml) holding only the fields, hand,
  card preview and prompt; written on first use and selected per match
  while "Board-First Match Layout" is on.
- ArenaRail: slim left column with Stack / Combat / Log toggles (stack
  count badge) and the tool dock; ArenaDrawer slides those panels out
  over the board.
- Player plates on each board: round avatar with life badge and
  targeting ring, name, compact zone counters, mana and extra counters
  only when non-zero. PlayArea keeps a strip free for the plate and caps
  card size.
- One horizontal phase bar above your board showing the stops for the
  player whose turn it is, with a switch for other players' stops.
- Prompt shown as an action plate; cell tabs and outlines hidden.
- Summary feed and stack cascade moved clear of the plates and bar.
